---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('brevo')!;
const path = '/apps/brevo';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/brevo');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/brevo');

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Which Shopify integration should I evaluate?",
    "answer": "Brevo currently documents Brevo PushOwl as the supported Shopify connection. Confirm the selected account and plan before importing into an existing Brevo database."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Brevo support Shopify browsing workflows?",
    "answer": "The current integration guide advertises browse abandonment and back-in-stock automation as well as cart and welcome flows. Verify your required events and rules in the selected app and plan."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I combine email, SMS, push and WhatsApp?",
    "answer": "Brevo PushOwl advertises those channels. Confirm country availability, permissions, credits and plan scope separately for each channel."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is an email subscriber automatically eligible for SMS?",
    "answer": "No. Keep permissions and eligibility separate for each channel and have the intended message reviewed for its destination."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will importing Shopify customers preserve every existing value?",
    "answer": "Do not assume so. Brevo warns that Shopify import can override customer attributes including subscription status. Review conflicting sample records before enabling campaigns."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Brevo send a digital course access email?",
    "answer": "Brevo provides SMTP and API delivery. A developer must implement the access-message caller and validate activation, retries and duplicate-event handling."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does installing the app replace Shopify receipts?",
    "answer": "Do not assume that it does. Inventory notification ownership and verify the intended receipt path separately from marketing workflows."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a Shopify quote include?",
    "answer": "Request the relevant app plan, contact and send limits, channel credits, transactional traffic, users, support and peak-month treatment. The budget examples here are not supplier prices."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should a store replace Brevo?",
    "answer": "Evaluate an alternative when a demonstrated requirement or total operating cost remains unacceptable after configuration and support review. Order count alone is not a migration rule."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">← All app reviews</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Shopify procurement review</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Choose the Shopify connection before the sending plan</h2>
      <p>Brevo is worth evaluating when the same operations team coordinates store campaigns and application messages across several markets. Its current Shopify route is Brevo PushOwl; a standalone Brevo account and the Shopify app should not be treated as interchangeable purchases. Start with the connection, the channels and the people who will operate them.</p>
      <p>Brevo’s connection guide identifies Brevo PushOwl as the supported replacement for the former Shopify app. It describes customer, product, collection and order sync, a storefront tracker, product blocks, and welcome, browse, cart and back-in-stock automations. Include these ecommerce workflows in the evaluation rather than assuming another supplier is required.</p>
      <p>This review uses supplier documentation checked November 25, 2026 and proposed procurement exercises. The European home goods, digital course and apparel examples below are acceptance cases, not stores we operated. No recovery rate, launch time or deliverability improvement was measured.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Import authority: who can overwrite a subscriber?</h2>
      <p>The connection guide warns that importing Shopify data makes Shopify the customer-data authority and can overwrite Brevo attributes, including subscription status. Before connecting an established account, export the current status and source for a small review sample. Include an email subscriber, an unsubscribed customer, a purchaser without marketing permission and a customer whose phone permission differs from email.</p>
      <p>Write an expected before-and-after record for each sample. Have the store administrator approve which system should win when values conflict. Keep campaigns paused until the actual sync agrees with that decision; a record appearing in a contact list is not permission to send every channel.</p>
      <p>For an international home goods catalogue, retain the original signup wording, language, source and available confirmation evidence alongside the mapped attributes. A country value is useful for routing but does not prove permission. Ask the privacy reviewer to assess the intended processing and contract; regional familiarity alone does not establish compliance or data residency.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Regional service and channel procurement</h2>
      <p>Build a market-by-channel sheet before buying credits: destination, language, sender identity, permitted audience, message purpose, local review owner and support contact. Separate an urgent service update from a promotional restock invitation even when both concern the same product. Ask the supplier to confirm support hours and escalation coverage for the store’s actual operating regions.</p>
      <p>Brevo documents country-dependent SMS credit consumption and a destination calculator. Quote the intended message and destination mix rather than multiplying every phone number by one universal rate. Ask how longer or translated messages affect the payable units, and verify sender registration and availability before promising a launch date.</p>
      <p>Brevo PushOwl advertises email, SMS, push and WhatsApp. That product scope is a reason to investigate coordinated campaigns, not proof that every plan, country or customer is eligible for all four. Require a written feature and quota matrix for the selected subscription. An email opt-in should not silently become a phone or browser permission.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Four proposed Shopify acceptance cases</h2>
      <p>Home goods welcome: use a German-language signup and a separate English signup. Confirm the permission state before enabling welcome, check the selected product block and fallback language, and unsubscribe while a later message is waiting. Pass evidence is the correct recipient and language plus suppression of the pending promotion; there is no promised confirmation rate.</p>
      <p>Cart recovery: stage a €72 cart, then complete the purchase before a delayed reminder. Also change quantity and remove an item in separate rehearsals. Inspect the actual checkout link, current product details and pending sends. Name the operator who can stop the reminder if the purchase event arrives late. A successful preview alone does not prove purchase suppression.</p>
      <p>Digital course: keep Shopify’s receipt owner explicit, then evaluate Brevo SMTP or API for a separate course-access message. Replay the purchase callback and revoke access on a refund in the course system. Confirm one access message, a working login destination and a retry record; do not assume installing the marketing connector replaces Shopify receipts or provisions the course.</p>
      <p>Apparel reorder: choose an item with a plausible replacement interval and a second item that should never receive that reminder. Rehearse a return, a repeat purchase before the delay expires and a sold-out size. Inspect whether the required fields reach the workflow and whether the current app/plan can express the desired rules. Use the observed exceptions to decide configuration or development work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Separate marketing operations from transactional callers</h2>
      <p>Brevo offers SMTP and API delivery for transactional messages, with a separate activation step documented for custom integrations. That capability can serve a digital store’s application messages while campaign operators use marketing tools. It does not mean a marketing plan automatically includes every transactional requirement or that the Shopify connector takes over order notifications.</p>
      <p>Create a message inventory with one producing system and one owner per purpose: receipt, access link, shipping update, welcome and upsell. The application developer owns retry handling and duplicate-event protection; the campaign operator owns promotional eligibility. Treat an API success response as submission evidence and inspect delivery/error logs separately.</p>
      <p>Use separate sender identities or subdomains where the operating design calls for them, authenticate them and monitor each stream. Separation helps diagnosis; it does not guarantee inbox placement or eliminate reputation interactions. Keep a tested fallback for course access if the delivery service or application queue fails.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Queue control and rollback before a channel launch</h2>
      <p>A multichannel sequence needs an offer owner. Document what happens when a welcome message, a cart reminder and a restock alert become eligible together. Rehearse a recent purchase and a fresh unsubscribe between scheduling and dispatch. Record which queues can be cancelled, which messages have already left, and who can pause each channel.</p>
      <p>If moving from an older connector, first inventory forms, trackers, legacy flows, sender identities and outstanding credits. Capture pending recipients before disabling anything. Pause the old trigger, reconcile its queue, then enable the replacement for the agreed cohort. Do not run overlapping recovery messages merely to compare dashboards.</p>
      <p>Rollback should restore the intended trigger without replaying messages already sent by the replacement. Preserve a dispatch ledger and a support ticket template containing timestamps, customer identifiers and the affected workflow, with access limited to the people investigating.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Plan economics: quote the whole workload</h2>
      <p>The Brevo PushOwl pricing page is the relevant starting point for Shopify subscriptions; Brevo’s general platform pricing is a separate reference. Obtain a dated quote covering contacts, campaign and automation sends, channel credits, user access, reporting, support and transactional traffic. Confirm whether quotas are shared, separate or capped, including the behavior at exhaustion.</p>
      <p>Illustrative workload, not a supplier quote: 14,200 stored customers with 8,000 permitted campaign recipients receiving three campaigns produces 24,000 campaign sends. Add 4,000 automation messages for 28,000 marketing emails. Budget 12,000 application messages separately until the vendor confirms the contract and quota treatment. Stored customers and sendable recipients are different quantities.</p>
      <p>For a hypothetical proposal, allow $120 monthly for software and credits and six operator hours at $35: total operating cost is $330. An alternative budget of $170 plus three hours at $35 totals $275. The higher license allowance is $55 cheaper overall in this example; neither number is a Brevo price. Include import cleanup and peak-month volume before comparing annual totals.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Contribution sensitivity without an invented uplift</h2>
      <p>For a $52 order at a hypothetical 48% contribution margin before campaign costs, contribution is $24.96. A $100 additional channel budget needs five additional orders to exceed that expense: four contribute $99.84 and five $124.80. Subtract discounts, fulfillment changes and returns if the margin assumption excludes them.</p>
      <p>Do not count every attributed order as incremental. Define the measurement window and an appropriate comparison cohort with the analyst before launch. If observed incremental contribution does not cover channel and operating costs, revise the offer or stop that channel; this does not automatically require replacing the whole platform.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Renewal and handoff based on actual service requirements</h2>
      <p>Review import exceptions, channel credit consumption by destination, delayed receipt/access incidents, suppression failures and operator time. Add a region or channel only after someone owns its copy, permissions and escalation. Compare the selected plan’s reporting with the questions finance actually asks.</p>
      <p>Retain Brevo when the implemented workflows and service arrangement meet those requirements at an acceptable total cost. Investigate alternatives when a demonstrated requirement remains unresolved after configuration and support review. There is no order-count graduation rule, prescribed replacement vendor or universal recovery target.</p>
      <p>The handoff should contain the authoritative customer fields, channel matrix, workflow entry/exit rules, queue pause steps, application caller owner and renewal assumptions. A new operator should be able to stop a mistaken campaign without disabling a necessary course-access message.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Related reviews and guides</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps">All Shopify email apps</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/guides/pricing-models">Pricing models</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-mailchimp">Omnisend vs Mailchimp</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/mailchimp">Mailchimp review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify my-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Supplier references</h2>
      <p>Checked November 25, 2026. These describe advertised product behavior, not independently measured merchant performance. Confirm the current contract and account configuration before purchase.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">Brevo Shopify connection</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://www.pushowl.com/pricing">Shopify app plans</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/208717449-Supported-countries-and-pricing-for-SMS-messages">SMS destinations and pricing</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/7924148470546-How-can-I-send-transactional-emails-with-Brevo">Transactional sending</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000188150-Troubleshooting-Issues-with-Brevo-SMTP">SMTP activation troubleshooting</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Brevo Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
